Kernel_executeUserOp
├── when the caller is not the EntryPoint
│   └── when the caller is not the account itself
│       └── it should revert with Unauthorized error
└── when the caller is the EntryPoint or self
    ├── given no validation hook is set in transient storage
    │   ├── it should skip the preHook call
    │   ├── it should execute the inner callData via delegatecall
    │   └── it should skip the postHook call
    ├── given a validation hook is set in transient storage
    │   ├── it should call preHook on the hook contract with callData
    │   ├── given preHook reverts
    │   │   └── it should propagate the revert
    │   └── given preHook succeeds
    │       ├── it should execute the inner callData via delegatecall
    │       ├── given the inner execution reverts
    │       │   └── it should propagate the revert message
    │       └── given the inner execution succeeds
    │           ├── it should call postHook on the hook contract with context
    │           ├── given postHook reverts
    │           │   └── it should propagate the revert
    │           └── given postHook succeeds
    │               └── it should complete successfully
    ├── when the inner callData is execute with single call
    │   ├── it should execute the target call
    │   └── it should return the call result
    ├── when the inner callData is execute with batch calls
    │   ├── it should execute all calls in order
    │   └── it should return all results
    └── when the inner callData is execute with delegatecall
        ├── it should delegatecall to the target
        └── it should return the delegatecall result
